WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:00.700
Now, as

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.402
Russia faces widespread condemnation

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.803
over its war in Ukraine,

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.238
Cuba has emerged

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.941
as one of Moscow's biggest supporters.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.443
The two countries, both are subject to US

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.345
sanctions are seeking to deepen

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.179
economic ties

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.848
through trade and investment.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.815
CNN's Patrick

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.752
Oppmann reports now from Havana.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:22.022
A Russian warship sails in Havana,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.290
Cuba, greets the ship the Periscope,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.892
the first Russian naval vessel

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.961
to make an official visit in years

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.663
with a cannon fire salute.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.066
It's just the latest sign

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.768
of the forging of ties

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.770
between Russia and Cuba.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.971
Well, much of the rest of the world

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.172
has denounced Russia

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.907
for their invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.143
Cuban President Miguel Diaz-Canel,

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.277
seen here alongside

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.211
Vladimir Putin

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.313
inaugurating a statue of Fidel Castro

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.882
in Moscow in November,

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.118
defends Russia's war on the ground.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.320
We are saying we are condemning

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.489
we are rejecting the expansion of Miro

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.158
towards Russia's borders,

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:59.759
he told Russia today.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.295
We condemn all the measures and sanctions

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.197
that have been applied as a way

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.966
to coerce the Russian Federation.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:07.534
In Russia,

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.435
increasingly is

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.703
throwing a lifeline to their old ally

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.872
just 90 miles from the United States.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:14.307
Since the

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:14.641
war in

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.309
Ukraine began, Russia and Cuba

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.478
have signed a flurry of new agreements

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.846
that would open the four supermarkets

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.247
selling Russian food here,

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.183
increased oil shipments to the island.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.185
Even developed this beachside community

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.586
outside of Havana.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.621
It appears to be the most significant

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.957
Russian investment in Cuba in decades.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.794
In February, after Russia donated 25,000

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.262
tons of wheat, Russia's

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.964
then ambassador to Cuba

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:41.234
said the aid will continue to flow okay.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.068
Cuba.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.838
In spite of the challenges, he says,

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.539
Russia and Cuba

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.907
continue developing

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.642
their strategic relationship

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.311
based on the historic friendship,

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.513
solidarity and mutual sympathy

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.715
between our two countries.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.083
Some of the Soviet thinking came

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.685
the warming of ties for many Cubans

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.854
feels like a trip back to the future.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.123
In this video from the 1960s

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.058
narrated by Fidel Castro.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.326
Cubans are told how visiting

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.494
Russian experts

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.362
would modernize the island

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.296
Instead, Cuba grew

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.599
dependent on Soviet aid.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.968
The USSR collapsed and facing

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.437
punishing U.S. economic sanctions.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.906
The island plunged into a financial abyss

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:22.375
from which it is yet to emerge.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:22.876
Well, Russian

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:23.977
officials have suggested

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.879
reestablishing a military presence

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.913
on the island.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.581
Some analysts feel that Moscow

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.683
no longer has the capability to do so.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.952
I think this kind of threats

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:33.520
are used

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.089
more for taunting the United States

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.190
and for kind of

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.392
for war

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:39.893
is a kind of

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.326
a form

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.294
of psychosis,

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.595
psychological warfare,

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.964
kind of psyop against the United States.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.267
Whatever the future of the renewed ties.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.301
It's clear

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.802
Russia is once again

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.772
staking a claim in Cuba.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.507
Patrick Oppmann, CNN, Havana.

